According to the 2023 Customs Post Clearance Audit Manual, the auditors are required to maintain a "Working Paper" for each transaction that details the following:

(a) A summary of the work performed;
(b) The results of the work, i.e. the findings obtained through the applied procedures; 
(c) The decisions made based on the findings; and
(d) The issues and recommendations for the audited person/entity.

The Working Paper must be comprehensive, accurate, and logically structured to support the audit report and facilitate future audits.

According to Clause 9 of Document 1, the Commissioner of Customs (Bond) or the authorized Commissioner of Customs can issue a certificate to the Customs House Commissioner or the Customs Station Controlling Commissioner for the release of the imported goods, provided that the importer submits the following information:

(a) LC number;
(b) B/L or Airway Bill number or Truck Receipt number;
(c) Invoice number; and
(d) Description and quantity of the goods.

According to Clause 5 of the Customs Rules 2024, the following documents are required for filing a Utilization Declaration (UD) for obtaining goods from a bonded warehouse for export purposes:

(a) One copy each of the buyer's letter of credit (master export letter of credit), contract, and purchase order;
(b) Proforma invoice;
(c) Sketch of the garments to be exported; and
(d) Up-to-date copy of the general bond.

